Peptide OmniPanel — Third-Party Notices & Research Scope Statement
==================================================================

1. Scientific & Regulatory Scope Disclaimer
-------------------------------------------
Peptide OmniPanel is an academic research platform intended strictly for
early-stage preclinical hypothesis generation and compound prioritization
(`internal_research_only`). Predictions, uncertainty intervals, structural
saliency maps, and linked regulatory label records MUST NOT be used for
clinical diagnosis, patient dosing, medical decision-making, or regulatory
submissions.

2. Regulatory Clinical PK Reference Panel (`web/clinical_evidence_index.json`)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The Clinical & Regulatory PK panel displays factual numeric/range human PK
parameters for marketed FDA-approved peptide drugs paired with direct links
to official NLM DailyMed SPL documents (`setid` resolved directly via the
public NLM DailyMed v2 REST API, https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/) and US FDA
Drugs@FDA NDA/BLA Clinical Pharmacology Reviews (https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/).

Legal & provenance distinction:
- Scientific numeric PK measurements are factual data.
- US FDA NDA/BLA Clinical Pharmacology Reviews authored by FDA staff are US
  Federal Government works (17 U.S.C. § 105).
- DailyMed SPL documents contain manufacturer-submitted prescribing
  information distributed via NLM DailyMed; no narrative label text is
  reproduced.
- Initial drug-list and numeric PK pre-selection drew from public FDA label
  extractions (including ADMETatlas V1.0), after which ALL CC-BY-NC derivative
  fields (FAERS summaries, clinical trial aggregations, narrative annotations,
  and `ATLPD*` identifiers) were stripped from the working tree and `main`
  branch history via `git-filter-repo`, legacy remote branches were deleted,
  and 53/59 products were verified live against official NLM DailyMed v2 REST
  API `setid` records (87.3% exact numeric match in live SPL text). A fresh
  zero-history release archive will be minted for final manuscript submission
  to ensure zero residual GitHub orphan-commit cache.

3. Public Repository Data Redistribution Policy & Live Analog Notice
--------------------------------------------------------------------
This public repository distributes original source code, audited evaluation
manifests, reproducible audit scripts, aggregate corpus statistics
(`data/peptide_ml_cleaning_v1_statistics_v1/` and
`data/peptide_pk_literature_round1/audit_report.json`), and the factual FDA
regulatory PK lookup table above. Raw row-level third-party observation tables
(e.g., CycPeptMPDB, DBAASP, PEPlife2, THPdb, ChEMBL, SweMacrocycleDB) are NOT
redistributed in this repository; researchers must obtain raw datasets directly
from their respective primary portals under upstream terms documented in
`DATA_LICENSES.md`. The hosted web API's `nearest_analogs` readout displays
up to 3 nearest training compounds solely for non-commercial academic
applicability-domain inspection.

